  "body": "**Stacked on #502** (chamfer/deburr edge breaks). Its commits show here until #502 merges; this PR adds one commit on top.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe program sim forgave convicted columns down to a cached edge-break record's depth. The record is file data, so a hand-edited or corrupted project could state any depth and hide a real gouge under an inflated bevel (review note on #502). Each op's records are now held to the break width its own params state: `Chamfer2D` / `Deburr` `width`, against the record's `depth / slope`, with a micron of lattice slack. A wider record, or a record on a kind that declares no break, is dropped with a logged warning, and its columns are judged against the sharp model: stricter, never looser. The bound sits where the sim reads each op's records (`stock_sim::breaks::bounded`), so a fresh generation and a loaded file are judged alike.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `edge_break_bound`, 3/3:\n  - `an_inflated_record_no_longer_forgives_a_deeper_cut`: a chamfer ridden 0.3 mm deep, saved, its break depth hand-scaled ×5 in the file and reloaded. It still convicts.\n  - `an_unedited_file_still_credits_its_own_break`\n  - `the_bound_reads_the_ops_own_width`\n- With the call site reverted, the first test fails (\"the inflated record forgave a real gouge\"). That is the bug.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`, escalated to batch, 906 s: every crate suite is green, including #502's `edge_break_gate`, `deburr_links` and every stock_sim-mapped suite. Clippy `-D warnings` is clean on all 8 crates. ui: only the three known GPU-adapter reds that are also red on main.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA GUI view. The change only narrows what the verify credits.\n\nChangelog: The gouge check credits a chamfer's or deburr's declared edge break only within the width the operation states, so a hand-edited project cannot widen it (#529)\n\nFixes #529\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
